  "worked_solution": "The word \"and\" is represented by the symbol \"$\\land$\", while the word \"or\" is represented by the symbol \"$\\lor$\".\n\nNote that this sentence consists of two parts:\n\n- **Part 1:** $9$ is a perfect square. This corresponds to $P.$\n\n- **Part 2:** $ 3 \\geq 4$ or $3= 5-1.$ This corresponds to\n\\[\n\\underbrace{3 \\geq 4 }_Q \\quad \n\\underbrace{\\vphantom{p}\\textbf{or}}_{\\lor} \\quad \\underbrace{3= 5-1 }_R,\n\\]\nthat is, $Q \\lor R.$\n\nSo, we can express the sentence as\n\\[\n\\underbrace{9 \\vphantom{p}\\textrm{ is a perfect square} }_P \\quad \\underbrace{\\vphantom{p}\\textbf{or}}_{\\lor} \\quad \n\\underbrace{3 \\geq 4 \\textbf{ or } 3=5-1 }_{Q \\, \\lor \\, R},\n\\]\nthat is, $P \\lor (Q \\lor R).$",
