  "html": "<div id=\"questionExplanation-178520\" class=\"questionExplanation\" style=\"display: block;\"><p>The word \"and\" is represented by the symbol \"$\\land$\", while the word \"or\" is represented by the symbol \"$\\lor$\".</p>\n<p>Note that this sentence consists of two parts:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><p><strong>Part 1:</strong> $9$ is a perfect square. This corresponds to $P.$</p>\n</li>\n<li><p><strong>Part 2:</strong> $ 3 \\geq 4$ or $3= 5-1.$ This corresponds to\n\\[\n\\underbrace{3 \\geq 4 }_Q \\quad \n\\underbrace{\\vphantom{p}\\textbf{or}}_{\\lor} \\quad \\underbrace{3= 5-1 }_R,\n\\]\nthat is, $Q \\lor R.$</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>So, we can express the sentence as\n\\[\n\\underbrace{9 \\vphantom{p}\\textrm{ is a perfect square} }_P \\quad \\underbrace{\\vphantom{p}\\textbf{or}}_{\\lor} \\quad \n\\underbrace{3 \\geq 4 \\textbf{ or } 3=5-1 }_{Q \\, \\lor \\, R},\n\\]\nthat is, $P \\lor (Q \\lor R).$</p>\n<div class=\"studentAnswerHeader\">Your Answer:</div><div class=\"studentAnswer\">$R \\land (P \\lor Q)$</div></div>",
